\section*{The exact weak-recovery threshold for the symmetric three-community SBM}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a mathematical result relevant to this question in the selected manuscript. Three-state symmetric broadcasting is claimed reconstructible precisely when $d\lambda^2>1$ on regular and observed Poisson trees, for both signs of the channel parameter.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} The tree channel has three equally likely states and transition matrix with diagonal \((1+2\lambda)/3\) and off-diagonal \((1-\lambda)/3\), so \(-1/2\le\lambda\le1\). On a regular tree with branching \(b\ge2\), or a Poisson Galton--Watson tree of mean \(d>1\), the claim gives
\[
 \text{reconstruction}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad d\lambda^2>1,
 \qquad d=b\text{ in the regular case},
\]
with nonreconstruction at admissible equality. The SBM corollary fixes \(a,b>0\), \((a+2b)/3>1\), assigns independent uniform labels in \(\{1,2,3\}\), and uses edge probabilities \(a/n\) within a label and \(b/n\) across labels. For overlap maximized over label permutations, it claims
\[
 (a-b)^2\le3(a+2b)\ \Longrightarrow\
 \mathbb E\operatorname{ov}(\sigma,\widehat\sigma_n)\to1/3
\]
for every estimator from the graph and independent randomness. Under the strict reverse inequality, some \(O(n\log n)\) algorithm achieves overlap at least \(1/3+\varepsilon\) with probability tending to one. These SBM statements retain the mean-degree assumption. Reconstruction means $\lim_{\ell\to\infty}a_\ell>0$, where
\[
 a_\ell=\mathbb E\left\|\mathbb P(\sigma_{\varnothing}\in\cdot\mid T_{\le\ell},\sigma_{\partial T_\ell})-\operatorname{Unif}\{1,2,3\}\right\|_{\mathrm{TV}}.
\]
The tree shape in the conditioning is unlabelled. In the Galton--Watson case the expectation includes extinct trees; it is not conditioned on survival.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
The posterior is represented by a complex mean and two invariant statistics. Fixed-point inequalities separately exclude positive and negative threshold reconstruction, and an exact finite certificate treats the coloring boundary; known transfer theorems then give the corresponding three-community graph recovery threshold.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The SBM corollary uses iid uniform latent labels (equal class sizes in expectation), positive fixed a,b and mean offspring d=(a+2b)/3>1. It does not state the exact-balanced class-size conditioning or all parameter regimes of this target. This entry records partial support; complete coverage of the question is not established by this catalogue.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 229, the three-state Comparator entries only establish reconstruction when $d\lambda^2>1$. They omit threshold nonreconstruction, the graph recovery corollary, and the four-state companions. The listed Comparator files are \texttt{ThreeStateSupercritical.lean}, \texttt{ThreeStateTreeClauses.lean}. The inventory does not supply a named declaration for these Comparator entries. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
